{"id":"h6-03-p3","title":"Design a key-value store (Dynamo-style)","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: partitioning, replication, quorums, vector clocks, hinted handoff, anti-entropy, LSM storage. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"requirements","title":"Requirements","html":"<p><strong>A key-value store maps a key to a value: <code>put(key, value)</code> and <code>get(key)</code>.</strong> A Dynamo-style store does this across many machines, always writable, and tolerates failures. Amazon's Dynamo paper (2007) inspired Cassandra, Riak and DynamoDB. The shopping cart is the classic use: never refuse an \"add to cart\".</p>\n<p><strong>Functional</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>put(key, value)</code>, <code>get(key)</code>, <code>delete(key)</code>.</li>\n<li>Values are opaque blobs, small (under 1 MB, typically 1 to 10 KB).</li>\n<li>Optional: TTL, conditional writes.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Non-functional</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Highly available for writes (no single leader that blocks writes).</li>\n<li>Horizontally scalable: add nodes, data rebalances.</li>\n<li>Low latency: p99 under 10 ms.</li>\n<li>Tunable consistency (eventual by default, stronger when requested).</li>\n<li>Survives node, rack and even data-centre failure.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 455.2 192\" width=\"455.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Shape of the system\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M297.2 96 L353.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M297.2 96 L353.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M297.2 96 L353.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M297.2 96 L353.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M297.2 96 L353.2 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M297.2 96 L353.2 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Coordinator node</text><rect x=\"353.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"398.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica 1</text><rect x=\"353.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"398.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica 2</text><rect x=\"353.2\" y=\"136\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"398.2\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica 3</text></svg><figcaption>Shape of the system</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> The big choice is CAP: Dynamo picks availability over strict consistency (AP). That is a one-way door for the data model: if you later need strong cross-key transactions you need a different system (Spanner, a relational DB). Reversible within the system by tuning quorum per request.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A phone book copied into three offices; any office can add a number, and they sync up later.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Not stating CAP preference and consistency model.</li>\n<li>Proposing a single master and calling it highly available.</li>\n<li>Confusing this with a cache (it must be durable).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"api","title":"API","html":"<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">PUT /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/kv/{</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">key</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Headers: X-Consistency: quorum | one | all   (optional, default quorum)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">         If-Match: &#x3C;version-context>          (optional, for read-modify-write)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"value\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"&#x3C;base64 bytes>\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"ttlSeconds\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">86400</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> OK</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"version\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"[(nodeA,3),(nodeB,1)]\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }       </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// vector clock context</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">503</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Service Unavailable -> could not reach enough replicas</span></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">GET /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/kv/{</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">key</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}?consistency=quorum</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> OK  { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"values\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [ {</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"value\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"&#x3C;b64>\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"context\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"[(A,3),(B,1)]\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">} ] }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// More than one entry in \"values\" means conflicting siblings: the client merges.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">404</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Not Found</span></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">DELETE /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/kv/{</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">key</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}   -> </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">204</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (writes a tombstone)</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Client-side library does the real work: it knows the ring, picks a coordinator and retries. Internal node-to-node RPCs: <code>replicate(key, value, clock)</code>, <code>read(key)</code>, <code>hint(key, value, forNode)</code>, <code>gossip(state)</code>, <code>merkleRoot(range)</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry example.</strong> DynamoDB exposes <code>PutItem</code>/<code>GetItem</code> with <code>ConsistentRead</code> flag; Cassandra exposes consistency levels <code>ONE</code>, <code>QUORUM</code>, <code>ALL</code> per query.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A form where you tick \"tell me when 2 of the 3 offices have it\".</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Not exposing what happens on conflicts (siblings, last-write-wins).</li>\n<li>Forgetting deletes need tombstones in an eventually consistent store.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"estimates","title":"Estimates","html":"<p>Assume 10B keys, average value 1 KB, replication factor N = 3, 200k ops/s peak (80% reads).</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Quantity</th>\n<th>Calculation</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Raw data</td>\n<td>10B x 1 KB</td>\n<td>10 TB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>With replicas</td>\n<td>x3</td>\n<td>30 TB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Per node (say 2 TB usable, 50% headroom)</td>\n<td>30 TB / 1 TB used</td>\n<td>~30 nodes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Write rate</td>\n<td>40k/s x 3 replicas</td>\n<td>120k replica writes/s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Per node</td>\n<td>120k / 30</td>\n<td>~4k writes/s plus reads, easy for SSD + LSM</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Index memory (bloom + index)</td>\n<td>~10 bits per key per node</td>\n<td>10B x 3 x 10 bits / 8 = ~37 GB total, ~1.2 GB/node</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Start with 36 nodes in 3 racks for headroom. Disk is the constraint, not CPU.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 656.4 68\" width=\"656.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Capacity logic\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 34 L164 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 34 L164 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M267.2 34 L323.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M267.2 34 L323.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M413.2 34 L469.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M413.2 34 L469.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">10 TB data</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">x3 replicas</text><rect x=\"323.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"368.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">30 TB</text><rect x=\"469.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"175.20000000000002\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"556.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">~36 nodes of 2 TB SSD</text></svg><figcaption>Capacity logic</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Working out how many filing cabinets you need if every file is stored in three copies.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Forgetting the replication factor in storage.</li>\n<li>Ignoring compaction headroom (LSM needs 30 to 50% free disk).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"high-level-design","title":"High-level design","html":"<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 565.2 192\" width=\"565.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Dynamo-style architecture\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M407.2 34 L463.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M407.2 34 L463.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M407.2 96 L463.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M407.2 96 L463.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Coordinator</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"362.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Node A</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"362.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Node B</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"136\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"362.2\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Node C</text><rect x=\"463.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"508.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Gossip</text></svg><figcaption>Dynamo-style architecture</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Building blocks (the Dynamo toolbox)</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Partitioning:</strong> consistent hashing ring with virtual nodes.</li>\n<li><strong>Replication:</strong> each key stored on the next N nodes clockwise on the ring (the preference list).</li>\n<li><strong>Consistency:</strong> quorums: W writes + R reads with R + W > N.</li>\n<li><strong>Versioning:</strong> vector clocks to detect conflicting writes.</li>\n<li><strong>Failure handling:</strong> sloppy quorum plus hinted handoff for temporary failures; Merkle trees for repair.</li>\n<li><strong>Membership:</strong> gossip protocol, no central master.</li>\n<li><strong>Storage engine per node:</strong> LSM tree (memtable, WAL, SSTables).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Any node can be the coordinator (client picks via the ring or any node forwards). No single point of failure.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Leaderless replication is the foundational choice: great availability, harder consistency. Alternative: single leader per partition (Raft, as in CockroachDB/Spanner/etcd), which gives linearizability but pauses writes during leader election. Choice is effectively a one-way door.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Cassandra and Riak copy the design; DynamoDB (the managed service) is Dynamo-inspired but internally uses leader-based Multi-Paxos per partition. Voldemort powered LinkedIn.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A team with no manager: anyone can take an order, and teammates tell each other the news.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying \"like Redis cluster\" (that has primaries and replicas, a different model).</li>\n<li>Not mentioning virtual nodes.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"deep-dives","title":"Deep dives","html":"<h3>Partitioning with consistent hashing</h3>\n<p>Hash the key (MD5/Murmur3) onto a ring 0 to 2^128. Each node owns the arc before it. Adding a node moves only about 1/N of keys, not all (modulo hashing would move almost everything).</p>\n<p><strong>Virtual nodes:</strong> each physical node takes 128 to 256 random points on the ring, so load is even and a failed node's data spreads over many neighbours instead of one. Heterogeneous machines take more vnodes.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 714 68\" width=\"714\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Key goes to the next node on the ring, then replicates onward\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M282.8 34 L338.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M282.8 34 L338.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M492.4 34 L548.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M492.4 34 L548.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Key hash</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"220.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Node A (owner)</text><rect x=\"338.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"415.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Node B (replica 2)</text><rect x=\"548.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"625.1999999999999\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Node C (replica 3)</text></svg><figcaption>Key goes to the next node on the ring, then replicates onward</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Worked example: 36 nodes x 256 vnodes = 9,216 ring points; losing one node redistributes its ~1/36 over many peers (about 2.8% of data), not onto a single neighbour.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Partition key and hash function are one-way: changing them rewrites all data. Number of vnodes is easy to tune early, painful later.</p>\n<h3>Replication and quorums</h3>\n<p>N = 3 replicas. A write succeeds after <strong>W</strong> acks, a read waits for <strong>R</strong> responses; R + W > N guarantees the read overlaps the latest write.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Config</th>\n<th>Behaviour</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>N=3, W=2, R=2</td>\n<td>Balanced default, tolerates 1 failure</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>W=1, R=3</td>\n<td>Fast writes, slow reads</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>W=3, R=1</td>\n<td>Fast reads, writes fail if any node is down</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>W=1, R=1</td>\n<td>Fastest, eventual consistency only</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 273.2 192\" width=\"273.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Write with W=2 of N=3\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Coordinator</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica 1</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica 2</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"136\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.2\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica 3</text></svg><figcaption>Write with W=2 of N=3</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Coordinator sends to all 3 and replies when 2 ack. Quorum does not equal linearizability: sloppy quorums, clock issues and concurrent writes can still return stale data.</p>\n<h3>Conflicts and vector clocks</h3>\n<p>Two clients update the same cart at the same time on different replicas. Which wins? A <strong>vector clock</strong> is a list of <code>(node, counter)</code> pairs attached to each version.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>v1: [(A,1)]                   cart = {milk}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>v2: [(A,2)]                   cart = {milk, eggs}      descends from v1</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>v3: [(A,1),(B,1)]             cart = {milk, bread}     concurrent with v2</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>v2 supersedes v1 (counters all greater or equal). v2 and v3 are concurrent: neither contains the other, so both are returned as <strong>siblings</strong> and the application merges (union of carts). Alternative: <strong>last-write-wins</strong> by timestamp (Cassandra default): simple but silently drops writes and relies on synced clocks. For counters/sets use CRDTs.</p>\n<p>Vector clocks grow with the number of writers; Dynamo truncates old entries (a rare loss of precision).</p>\n<h3>Handling failures: sloppy quorum and hinted handoff</h3>\n<p>If a replica is down, write to the next healthy node on the ring with a <strong>hint</strong> (\"this belongs to node C\"). When C returns, the holder hands the data back. This keeps writes available during failures at the cost of temporary inconsistency. Hints expire (for example 3 hours); longer outages need repair.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 490 192\" width=\"490\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Replica C is down, node D keeps its data temporarily\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M332 158 L388 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M332 158 L388 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Coordinator</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"251.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica A</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"251.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica B</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"136\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"251.6\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Node D (hint for C)</text><rect x=\"388\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"433\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica C</text></svg><figcaption>Replica C is down, node D keeps its data temporarily</figcaption></figure>\n<h3>Anti-entropy with Merkle trees</h3>\n<p>Replicas drift. Each node keeps a <strong>Merkle tree</strong> (a hash tree) per key range. Two replicas compare root hashes; if equal, in sync; if not, descend to find the differing leaves and sync only those. Cuts repair traffic from comparing billions of keys to a few hash exchanges. Cassandra runs <code>nodetool repair</code> for this and recommends it at least within <code>gc_grace_seconds</code> (default 10 days).</p>\n<h3>Membership and failure detection</h3>\n<p>No central master. Each node gossips its view of the cluster to a few random peers every second. Failure detection uses a phi-accrual detector (Cassandra) rather than a fixed timeout. New nodes contact seed nodes to join.</p>\n<h3>Storage engine: LSM tree</h3>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 475.6 130\" width=\"475.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"LSM write path: log, memory, flush to disk, compact\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M282.8 34 L338.8 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M282.8 34 L338.8 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Write</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Memtable</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"220.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">WAL (disk)</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"220.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">SSTable (disk)</text><rect x=\"338.8\" y=\"43\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"401.2\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Memtable (RAM)</text></svg><figcaption>LSM write path: log, memory, flush to disk, compact</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li>Append to the <strong>commit log (WAL)</strong> for durability, then insert into the in-memory <strong>memtable</strong>.</li>\n<li>When the memtable reaches ~64 MB, flush to an immutable sorted <strong>SSTable</strong>.</li>\n<li>Reads check memtable, then SSTables newest first, using <strong>Bloom filters</strong> to skip files that definitely lack the key.</li>\n<li>Background <strong>compaction</strong> merges SSTables, drops overwritten values and expired tombstones.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Why LSM: sequential writes are fast (write-heavy workloads). Cost: read amplification and compaction I/O (write amplification 10x+). B-trees (as in DynamoDB's older designs, Postgres) read well but write randomly.</p>\n<p><strong>Production incident pattern.</strong> Symptom: read latency climbs over days and disk fills. Metric: pending compactions and SSTable count per read. Cause: compaction falling behind or tombstone buildup. Fix: more compaction throughput, avoid delete-heavy patterns, repair on schedule.</p>\n<h3>Reads: read repair</h3>\n<p>When a quorum read sees different versions, the coordinator returns the newest and asynchronously writes it to stale replicas (\"read repair\"), so frequently read data heals itself.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Vector clocks are like two people editing a shared recipe on paper: if neither saw the other's edit, you need a human to merge them.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Believing R + W > N gives strong consistency in all cases.</li>\n<li>Using LWW without admitting lost updates.</li>\n<li>Forgetting tombstones, so deleted data comes back from a stale replica (\"zombie data\").</li>\n<li>Hot keys: one celebrity key overloads its 3 replicas; mitigate with caching or key splitting.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"what-interviewers-look-for","title":"What interviewers look for","html":"<ul>\n<li>Explicit CAP position and consistency knobs (N, R, W).</li>\n<li>The full toolbox: consistent hashing with vnodes, quorums, vector clocks, hinted handoff, Merkle trees, gossip.</li>\n<li>Why each exists: availability during failures, convergence afterwards.</li>\n<li>Storage engine understanding (LSM, WAL, bloom filters, compaction).</li>\n<li>Conflict resolution strategy and its cost (siblings vs LWW vs CRDT).</li>\n<li>Capacity numbers and rack/data-centre awareness (replicas on different racks and DCs).</li>\n<li>Seniors discuss hot partitions, rebalancing speed, cross-DC replication latency, tombstone/GC settings and compare with leader-based systems (Raft, Spanner).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Reciting Dynamo terms with no numbers or failure story.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Dynamo-style = leaderless, AP, always-writable KV store with tunable consistency.</li>\n<li>Partition by consistent hashing with virtual nodes; replicate to the next N nodes (N=3, different racks).</li>\n<li>Quorums (R + W > N) tune the latency/consistency trade; sloppy quorum + hinted handoff keep writes available.</li>\n<li>Vector clocks detect concurrent writes; app merges siblings, or accept last-write-wins and lost updates.</li>\n<li>Merkle trees and read repair converge replicas; gossip handles membership.</li>\n<li>Per-node storage is an LSM tree (WAL, memtable, SSTable, bloom filter, compaction).</li>\n<li>Choosing leaderless AP is a one-way door; quorum levels are per-request tunable.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}